the rise in hate crimes across the  country is growing a new report from the  fbi shows incidents up in 2020 13 more  than the year before matt kimbrough  joins us now in studio with more on how  the las vegas community is reacting to  this report  brian the fbi released its 2020 report  tonight now it shows that hate crimes  against african americans rose nearly 46  percent from 2019 and attacks on asian  americans grew by 73 percent we should  point out that while these numbers are  troubling many incidents don't even get  reported  no one should ever accept that hate  crimes are a part of life the fbi just  released updated numbers showing that  2020 saw the highest number of reported  hate crimes in two decades in total  nearly 62 percent of hate crimes  nationwide were tied to an individual's  race in nevada 113 incidents were  reported in 2020 compared to 47 in 2019  it's never a sign of weakness to say we  have a problem  it's a sign of weakness to ignore it  this past july a tick-tock video  surfaced of a woman at the shops at  crystals on the las vegas strip sounding  off in a racist rant making anti-asian  comments las vegas local rosita lee who  is part of the asian-american pacific  islander community says the lack of  progression we've made in these last  couple years is maddening as she has met  several people who don't come forward  after becoming victims of hate people  are  not reporting  we have found that many incidences  especially among the nurses i don't know  if you're aware but many of the nurses  are asians and there have been some  people  some patients who have said i don't want  you to treat me i want somebody else  now as we mentioned the report shows  more than half of victims in 2020 were  targeted because of their race 20  percent of people were victimized for  sexual orientation and 13 percent  because of religion back to you brian
 

